@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@email = prueba345@si.com
@password = 123456
@breedId = 1
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Obtain a token using an existing account
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### List pets (slides 4-7)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reject an empty payload (slide 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Create a pet using an existing breed ID (slide 6)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Luna",
  "breed": {{breedId}},
  "age": 3,
  "gender": "Female",
  "image": "",
  "status": "Available"
}

### Search by name (slides 8-11, case-sensitive LIKE on PostgreSQL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?q=Lu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Order by age ascending (slides 12-13)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?sort=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Order by age descending (slide 14)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?sort=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### First page, two pets per page (slides 15-24)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?page=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Second page
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Third page
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?page=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Combine pagination and search (slide 25)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?page=1&q=Lu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Combine pagination, search and age order (slide 26)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pet/back?page=1&q=Lu&sort=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
